I enter the cave of the Fortune Teller. It's filled with tons of nick-nacks and (random shit).
Jimmothy: Hello?
Fortune Teller: Hello young man! Sit, sit, and let me give you destiny's advice!
Fortune Teller: You must pay 300 gold to receive my services.
- *I Fork over the gold*
- Hell no! How about 20?
	Fortune Teller: How stingy! Fate has us here for a reason, but I don't appreciate your penniless behavior. 
I give her the gold and sit. She pulls out some kind of stone from behind her.
Fortune Teller: Here it is, my wonderous crystal ball. She's quite the beauty, isn't she?
- Jimmothy: Woah, it looks so tuff! + 5 aura
	Fortune Teller: Yes, yes. It has been passed down my lineage of Fortune Tellers for hundreds of years, in fact, I think- 
	Jimmothy: I didn't pay to hear your life story.
	Fortune Teller: Nevermind then...hmph.
- Jimmothy: Your crystal ball looks like a rock -10 aura
	Fortune Teller: Mind your language! Don't you dare refer to her as that again!
Fortune Teller: Hum.....Hum.....Hum.....
Jimmothy: Can you hurry this up?? I have dinner at 6.
Fortune Teller:  Patience young man, good things come to those who wait.
Jimmothy: I don't have time for your-
Fortune Teller: Aha! Here it is!
Fortune Teller: It's telling me...it's telling me....
Jimmothy: It's telling you i'm deaduzz going to leave.
Fortune Teller: Your future holds harsh trials and tribulations, but your love for others will give you the strength to move forward.
- Jimmothy: ...Is that it?
- Jimmothy: This reading is so lame. - 30 aura
	Jimmothy: Give me my money back or I'm giving this place a one star.
	Fortune Teller: How dare you insult the wisdom of my ancestors! Repent now or own up to your consequences.
	Jimmothy: Nah, I'd win.
	Fortune Teller: YOU'LL PAY FOR THIS.
	I get cursed and I shrivel up and die due to generational aura loss => END
Fortune Teller: Of course not!
Fortune Teller: Clocks will torment you for the rest of eternity if you don't be kind to one.
Jimmothy: Just to be clear, my future is dependent on whether or not I'm nice to a clock?
Fortune Teller: Now you get it! Don't make rude choices and think of your mother.
Fortune Teller: Our 7 minute session is over, thank you for choosing The Psychics Cave for your lifetime subscription of whimsy and luck. NO REFUNDS. AT ALL COSTS. Goodbye child!
